    "created_at": "2016-11-30T19:21:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-30T19:21:44Z",
    "body": "I think there is two parts to this: making BroadcastChannel work in opaque origins in chrome to communicate with other BroadcastChannel instances in the same realm should be possible (although annoying in that it requires a lot of code duplication in the implementation). Making it work so that different same (opaque) origin realms can talk with eachother is unlikely to be possible without a major rewrite of how opaque origins are treated in chrome. We just currently don't really have a way to express across threads/processes that two opaque origins are the same.\r\n\r\n(and since I just upstreamed chromes tests to wpt, they currently incorrectly test the existing ff/chrome behavior. In hindsight I should probably not have included that test in what I upstreamed).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
